**Repository reference:** https://github.com/mahimahfud-ui/Mahi-Remote-Control

**Design system:** Obsidian Telemetry

Mahi Remote Control is a cross-platform remote Android device access and control application.

It must provide two equally important controller options:

### MODE A — ANDROID PHONE → ANDROID PHONE

Phone A is the controller.

Phone B is the receiver.

Phone A must connect to Phone B, display its actual entire screen, and perform supported remote interactions.

### MODE B — BROWSER → ANDROID PHONE

A desktop or mobile browser acts as the controller.

The Android phone is the receiver.

The browser must display the actual receiver screen and support remote interaction.

### RECEIVER MODE — SHARE THIS PHONE

The same Android application must support receiver mode.

A receiver can generate a pairing code, authorize a controller, approve permissions, share its screen, and immediately terminate the connection.

These are two controller experiences connected to ONE unified Android receiver architecture.

Do not create separate incompatible screen-capture systems for the two modes.

